WEBVTT

00:02.043 --> 00:06.339
The four of us here
will stop Hakkai and destroy Taiju.

00:06.923 --> 00:11.344
Our secret battle is on December 25th,
Christmas night!

00:12.804 --> 00:14.347
Something's bothering me.

00:16.683 --> 00:20.145
I don't think
Mikey's going to last much longer.

00:20.228 --> 00:21.062
What?

00:21.563 --> 00:24.774
Baji's death is weighing him down,
but he acts like it doesn't bother him.

00:26.109 --> 00:27.986
-You're the one who killed--
-Chifuyu!

00:28.069 --> 00:31.531
If nothing changes,
Toman will be finished.

00:32.323 --> 00:34.117
We've got to give Mikey our support.

00:34.200 --> 00:38.163
We don't need
to work with you jerks to do that!

00:38.246 --> 00:39.622
Isn't that right, Takemitchy?

00:40.957 --> 00:43.668
We're keeping
this mission secret from Toman.

00:43.752 --> 00:46.004
So, I can't use anyone
in the Third or Sixth Division.

00:46.755 --> 00:49.674
That means we need you guys.

00:50.884 --> 00:51.718
Takemitchy,

00:52.802 --> 00:55.180
I hate wasting time.

00:56.097 --> 00:57.724
I want your answer by tomorrow.

01:08.526 --> 01:10.862
TOKYO REVENGERS

02:35.989 --> 02:37.448
I'm against it.

02:38.032 --> 02:40.451
Takemitchy,
we don't need to work with Kisaki!

02:40.535 --> 02:41.911
We can do this ourselves.

02:43.037 --> 02:44.164
Are you sure?

02:45.498 --> 02:48.793
He's the guy
who murdered Baji and Hinata Tachibana!

02:48.877 --> 02:50.211
Don't you get it?

02:50.295 --> 02:53.006
I do get it!
But what're we supposed to do?

02:56.217 --> 02:59.179
You want to kill Kisaki?
That's not the right thing to do!

02:59.929 --> 03:03.808
What we need to do
is kick Kisaki out of Toman!

03:03.892 --> 03:07.061
We also got to stop Hakkai
from killing Taiju!

03:07.645 --> 03:09.856
You think I like working with Kisaki?

03:09.939 --> 03:11.774
But if we work with him,

03:11.858 --> 03:14.277
then maybe
we can learn something about him!

03:14.360 --> 03:17.071
We might find a way to get him kicked out!

03:25.622 --> 03:26.664
I never...

03:27.332 --> 03:28.249
<i>ever want to see...</i>

03:29.167 --> 03:31.336
<i>that horrible future for everyone again.</i>

03:33.504 --> 03:36.716
To achieve that,
I'll even work with Kisaki.

03:37.300 --> 03:38.259
Please, Chifuyu.

03:39.636 --> 03:40.720
Work with me!

03:47.143 --> 03:48.436
Oh, jeez.

03:51.981 --> 03:54.943
I guess I've got no luck
with the chicks again this Christmas.

03:57.987 --> 03:59.072
Thank you, Chifuyu!

03:59.155 --> 04:00.823
You've got it good.

04:01.324 --> 04:02.659
You've got a girlfriend.

04:03.243 --> 04:04.827
Christmas sucks

04:04.911 --> 04:08.122
when I've got to work with bastards
to fight other bastards.

04:10.708 --> 04:11.668
Hey, you hungry?

04:23.721 --> 04:25.139
That didn't take long.

04:25.223 --> 04:26.641
You got an answer for me?

04:27.892 --> 04:31.104
We'll work with you guys
but only until Christmas.

04:32.188 --> 04:34.899
Smart decision. I appreciate it.

04:35.400 --> 04:38.069
All we want to do is protect Hakkai.

04:38.611 --> 04:40.697
We don't plan
on being friends with you guys.

04:48.579 --> 04:50.957
This is one screwed-up team.

04:52.583 --> 04:54.794
We're only here
because we have the same goal.

04:56.754 --> 04:59.674
I absolutely hate you guys's damn guts.

05:01.342 --> 05:03.303
What'll we call our team?

05:03.386 --> 05:04.846
"Season's Beatings?"

05:05.847 --> 05:07.515
Or how about "Hanmas?"

05:07.598 --> 05:10.101
Or "Team Massacre?" Like it?

05:17.984 --> 05:20.278
-See you later!
-Bye!

05:20.361 --> 05:22.363
-Bye!
-Okay. Talk to you later.

05:26.034 --> 05:28.911
<i>I never thought
I'd be working with Kisaki.</i>

05:29.454 --> 05:31.581
<i>But I could find out a lot
by working with him.</i>

05:31.664 --> 05:32.623
Takemichi!

05:33.374 --> 05:34.959
Let's walk home together.

05:35.043 --> 05:36.085
Hina!

05:36.169 --> 05:37.670
I'm here too.

05:39.714 --> 05:41.507
How'd your final exams go?

05:41.591 --> 05:43.760
What? Piece of cake!

05:43.843 --> 05:45.762
Really? I find that hard to believe.

05:47.972 --> 05:48.931
I can hardly wait.

05:49.432 --> 05:50.475
What?

05:50.558 --> 05:51.559
For Christmas.

05:54.228 --> 05:55.396
<i>Christmas?</i>

05:56.064 --> 05:58.691
<i>Did I promise
to do something with Hina on Christmas?</i>

05:59.650 --> 06:01.611
<i>Christ... mas!</i>

06:02.612 --> 06:05.907
<i>Wait! I'm double-booked that day!</i>

06:05.990 --> 06:07.950
<i>Oh, crap! What'll I do?</i>

06:09.535 --> 06:10.370
Hinata.

06:10.953 --> 06:12.497
I'm going home.

06:12.997 --> 06:14.665
I hate wasting time.

06:15.166 --> 06:16.542
Oh, okay.

06:16.626 --> 06:17.543
Jeez.

06:18.127 --> 06:21.464
I wish you wouldn't flirt
in front of your own brother.

06:22.131 --> 06:23.591
"Wasting time?"

06:24.592 --> 06:25.927
He sounds like Kisaki.

06:26.010 --> 06:27.762
Oh, it's nothing.

06:28.554 --> 06:31.265
I know what you mean.
That's just like him.

06:31.349 --> 06:33.142
-What?
-Yes?

06:34.852 --> 06:36.854
What did you just say?

06:36.938 --> 06:39.107
I said that's just like him.

06:40.733 --> 06:41.567
Like who?

06:43.444 --> 06:45.029
Tetta Kisaki, right?

06:47.573 --> 06:51.702
Hina, do you know... Kisaki?

06:51.786 --> 06:52.620
Yeah.

06:53.287 --> 06:55.665
We went to the same cram school
in elementary school.

06:55.748 --> 06:56.624
What?

06:56.707 --> 07:00.044
How come you know him, Takemichi?

07:02.422 --> 07:07.593
ADVANCED CLASS

07:07.677 --> 07:11.722
Let's look at the circumference of
a circle with a ten-centimeter diameter.

07:12.223 --> 07:16.602
If we draw a square around the outside
of the circle, it'll look like this.

07:16.686 --> 07:20.815
Then, this is what we get when
we put a right triangle along the radius.

07:28.156 --> 07:29.615
You're amazing, Kisaki!

07:31.200 --> 07:33.286
You placed first
on the practice exams again!

07:33.369 --> 07:34.704
NATIONAL ELEMENTARY SCHOOL TEST
1. TETTA KISAKI

07:34.787 --> 07:36.080
It was just luck.

07:36.164 --> 07:38.166
Wow! So humble!

07:40.460 --> 07:42.503
Your collar's crooked.

07:44.755 --> 07:46.090
There you go!

07:49.135 --> 07:50.386
Let's go, Hina.

07:53.931 --> 07:55.975
How can you talk to that guy?

07:56.058 --> 07:57.685
He's such a weirdo.

07:57.768 --> 08:00.855
What? How can you say that?
He's a good kid.

08:01.481 --> 08:06.486
Super-smart kids like that
seem to me like they've got no heart.

08:07.862 --> 08:12.074
Tetta Kisaki was the smartest kid
at cram school.

08:12.158 --> 08:16.120
Since we lived near him,
I sometimes walked home with him.

08:17.788 --> 08:21.250
<i>I never imagined
that Kisaki and Hina knew each other!</i>

08:21.334 --> 08:23.711
Then, he went to a private middle school,

08:23.794 --> 08:25.463
so I haven't seen him since then.

08:26.797 --> 08:29.008
He's a full-on gang member now.

08:29.091 --> 08:29.926
Really?

08:30.676 --> 08:32.678
He's a captain in Toman.

08:32.762 --> 08:34.639
No way! That's so not like him!

08:35.223 --> 08:36.057
It's the truth.

08:36.557 --> 08:38.768
And he's not your typical gang member.

08:39.268 --> 08:40.186
He's a real...

08:40.770 --> 08:42.063
Oh, never mind.

08:46.192 --> 08:49.570
But you know,
I think you and Kisaki would get along.

08:49.654 --> 08:50.571
What?

08:50.655 --> 08:54.075
He's a little awkward and blunt,

08:54.158 --> 08:55.826
but he's good at heart.

08:57.286 --> 08:59.413
<i>Tetta Kisaki's a good guy?</i>

08:59.497 --> 09:00.831
<i>That's impossible!</i>

09:00.915 --> 09:03.584
<i>He's a diabolical beast
who's murdered Hina over and over!</i>

09:04.085 --> 09:07.004
The first time I met you, Takemichi,

09:07.672 --> 09:09.590
I was with Kisaki.

09:09.674 --> 09:10.925
What? Really?

09:11.425 --> 09:14.095
What do you mean? When was that?

09:15.388 --> 09:16.973
You don't remember, do you?

09:17.056 --> 09:19.517
Huh? Remember what?

09:21.602 --> 09:23.729
I remember it very well.

09:25.982 --> 09:27.900
But I don't know...

09:28.985 --> 09:30.861
I don't really want to talk about it.

09:33.030 --> 09:34.532
Did something happen?

09:40.204 --> 09:43.374
It was the summer of sixth grade,
on the way home from cram school.

09:44.208 --> 09:46.627
Some kids were torturing a cat
in the park.

09:47.628 --> 09:52.592
That was the day
me and Kisaki first met you.

09:59.599 --> 10:01.976
-Come on! Let's hear you squeal more!
-More!

10:02.560 --> 10:04.186
I'm going to give them a tongue-lashing!

10:04.270 --> 10:05.563
Tachibana!

10:05.646 --> 10:07.773
It's no use. It's dangerous too.

10:09.275 --> 10:10.109
Tachibana!

10:10.735 --> 10:11.652
Take that!

10:11.736 --> 10:13.487
Cut that out! How dare you!

10:13.571 --> 10:15.114
What's so fun about that?

10:15.906 --> 10:16.824
What?

10:16.907 --> 10:18.284
Who's this brat?

10:18.367 --> 10:19.619
Mind your own business.

10:19.702 --> 10:22.747
Hey! The cat got away, damn it!

10:22.830 --> 10:26.000
Then, you'll have to take the cat's place.

10:26.083 --> 10:29.712
I hate brats like you,
acting all goody-two-shoes and shit.

10:31.130 --> 10:33.174
You going to cry?

10:33.257 --> 10:35.926
Think we'll let you off
'cause you're crying?

10:36.010 --> 10:39.013
Oh, man. I tried to stop her.

10:42.850 --> 10:43.726
What?

10:54.570 --> 10:57.657
The hero has arrived!

10:57.740 --> 10:59.450
I won't stand

10:59.533 --> 11:03.162
for some darn middle schoolers
ganging up on a little girl.

11:03.245 --> 11:05.081
What? Who's this brat?

11:05.164 --> 11:07.958
You can't be seriously
calling yourself a hero.

11:08.042 --> 11:10.294
This loser's wearing a cape!

11:10.378 --> 11:12.880
Look! He's shaking like a leaf!

11:13.881 --> 11:16.717
If you're that scared,
then quit acting like hot shit!

11:19.178 --> 11:20.429
Shut up!

11:34.902 --> 11:36.821
What're you crying for?

11:38.280 --> 11:39.198
I can't help it!

11:39.782 --> 11:41.283
You're weak, you know?

11:41.367 --> 11:43.994
You need to think
before you do stuff like this!

11:45.579 --> 11:46.455
I'm sorry...

11:48.833 --> 11:49.667
See you.

12:02.513 --> 12:06.183
What? Wait, was that really me?

12:06.267 --> 12:08.102
I don't remember that at all.

12:08.185 --> 12:12.732
But now that I think about it,
I may have done something like that.

12:13.399 --> 12:15.735
<i>I mean, that was 14 years ago now.</i>

12:16.235 --> 12:18.863
Dang, that was so lame.

12:19.405 --> 12:20.614
You think so?

12:20.698 --> 12:24.243
Of course!
I came to help but got my butt kicked.

12:24.827 --> 12:26.829
And where'd I get a cape?

12:27.663 --> 12:31.584
You came to help
even though you knew you'd lose.

12:31.667 --> 12:32.501
What?

12:33.127 --> 12:35.546
That's way more amazing
than someone who would've won.

12:39.258 --> 12:41.051
On that day,

12:42.136 --> 12:43.804
I fell in love with you.

12:49.518 --> 12:51.228
-Hanagaki.
-Huh?

12:51.312 --> 12:54.940
Tachibana in Class 2 says she likes you.

12:59.320 --> 13:00.446
Hello.

13:00.529 --> 13:01.655
Oh, hi.

13:02.198 --> 13:03.908
<i>For so long...</i>

13:04.492 --> 13:05.534
So...

13:06.869 --> 13:10.164
<i>...she's loved me?</i>

13:24.512 --> 13:25.679
Don't forget.

13:26.305 --> 13:28.766
We're meeting at Umishita Park
on Christmas Eve.

13:28.849 --> 13:29.725
Right.

13:31.519 --> 13:32.353
See you!

13:32.937 --> 13:35.606
<i>My fight with BLACK DRAGON
is coming up soon,</i>

13:35.689 --> 13:37.066
<i>so life's really tough now.</i>

13:38.400 --> 13:41.278
But I'm in seventh heaven!

13:41.862 --> 13:43.739
<i>Eve is the 24th, so it'll be fine.</i>

13:44.323 --> 13:46.826
<i>My battle is the next day,
the night of the 25th.</i>

13:47.409 --> 13:48.410
<i>I can do both!</i>

13:49.954 --> 13:50.788
Wait...

13:52.414 --> 13:54.917
<i>Christmas Eve... Umishita Park?</i>

13:56.210 --> 13:59.255
You dumped me here... on Christmas Eve.

14:01.841 --> 14:05.427
<i>Umishita Park is the place
Hina and I visited in the future.</i>

14:06.136 --> 14:08.055
<i>This year on Christmas Eve...</i>

14:08.722 --> 14:11.267
<i>I'm going to dump Hina!</i>

14:12.351 --> 14:13.686
But why?

14:14.186 --> 14:17.231
<i>There's no freaking way I'd dump Hina.</i>

14:19.733 --> 14:23.529
Yeah, that's right.
Christmas Eve is only a week away.

14:23.612 --> 14:27.324
Why the heck would I suddenly
want to dump her by then?

14:28.117 --> 14:29.702
Put it out of your mind.

14:29.785 --> 14:30.786
Hanagaki?

14:31.287 --> 14:33.289
What? Yeah?

14:33.372 --> 14:36.083
You're Takemichi Hanagaki, right?

14:37.751 --> 14:38.752
Naoto?

14:38.836 --> 14:40.796
It's nice to meet you, Hanagaki.

14:41.797 --> 14:44.675
I'm Masato Tachibana,
Hinata and Naoto's father.

14:45.175 --> 14:48.637
What? You're Hina's father?

14:49.680 --> 14:51.557
I'm sorry about that! Excuse me!

14:52.683 --> 14:53.559
COFFEE SHOP KOSHAKU

14:53.642 --> 14:55.477
I've heard a lot about you from my wife.

14:56.645 --> 14:58.147
You're dating my daughter, right?

14:58.230 --> 14:59.523
Yes!

14:59.607 --> 15:04.236
<i>Holy crap! It's her dad in the flesh!</i>

15:04.320 --> 15:06.822
<i>Even though I'm 26, I'm super tense!</i>

15:08.073 --> 15:09.491
Don't be so nervous.

15:10.075 --> 15:11.911
I'm not going to bite your head off.

15:11.994 --> 15:14.371
Oh... Well...

15:16.498 --> 15:20.044
I'm so busy,
I hardly ever have time for my children.

15:20.753 --> 15:22.796
I only ever hear about them from my wife.

15:23.297 --> 15:26.967
It's especially hard on Naoto,
so it's no wonder he hates my work.

15:27.676 --> 15:31.180
Since around the time he was born,
I've hardly ever been at home,

15:31.263 --> 15:33.766
so we haven't spent much time together.

15:34.975 --> 15:37.561
But the other day, he told me this.

15:38.062 --> 15:39.730
"I want to become a police officer."

15:42.191 --> 15:43.567
That's thanks to you, right?

15:43.651 --> 15:44.610
What?

15:44.693 --> 15:46.612
I don't know what you told him.

15:47.947 --> 15:49.615
But thank you. I'm very grateful.

15:49.698 --> 15:51.784
What? No, no! Not at all!

15:51.867 --> 15:53.452
I didn't do anything special!

15:53.535 --> 15:56.497
Please, you don't have to bow!

15:58.123 --> 16:00.376
I don't know
if he'll be fit for this work,

16:00.459 --> 16:02.586
but as his father, it made me happy.

16:03.170 --> 16:04.338
Oh, don't worry.

16:04.421 --> 16:06.006
Naoto will turn out to be a great cop--

16:06.090 --> 16:07.132
-What?
-What?

16:07.216 --> 16:08.342
Oh! It's nothing! Nothing at all!

16:10.427 --> 16:13.138
I'm glad you're as nice as I've heard.

16:13.222 --> 16:14.056
Huh?

16:14.890 --> 16:15.933
Hanagaki.

16:16.767 --> 16:18.894
Will you do me a favor?

16:18.978 --> 16:19.812
What?

16:21.563 --> 16:22.731
I'm home!

16:23.273 --> 16:25.776
Welcome home. Dinner's almost ready.

16:25.859 --> 16:26.860
Okay.

16:26.944 --> 16:28.654
Hinata was on a date.

16:28.737 --> 16:30.030
-Oh, really?
-Naoto!

16:31.907 --> 16:33.075
Mom.

16:33.158 --> 16:33.993
Yes?

16:34.076 --> 16:37.329
Mom, do you still love Dad even now?

16:38.872 --> 16:40.332
What kind of question is that?

16:41.333 --> 16:44.169
I was just wondering... how it really is.

16:46.130 --> 16:47.214
I love him very much.

16:49.466 --> 16:50.926
Ten years from now,

16:51.885 --> 16:53.721
I want to say the same about Takemichi!

16:54.555 --> 16:57.307
<i>The Kanto region
will remain mostly clear and sunny,</i>

16:57.391 --> 16:59.435
<i>but a cold front will move in next week.</i>

17:00.019 --> 17:03.605
<i>I guess that means
we could have a White Christmas, right?</i>

17:04.106 --> 17:06.066
<i>Yes, it's very likely.</i>

17:06.150 --> 17:09.653
<i>So stay warm and enjoy a lovely Christmas.</i>

17:10.487 --> 17:13.407
Please... break up with my daughter.

17:14.491 --> 17:16.869
I want her to be happy.

17:17.953 --> 17:19.413
Wait. Hold on here.

17:20.039 --> 17:21.373
But I'm in love with--

17:21.457 --> 17:22.541
You're a hoodlum.

17:24.084 --> 17:26.378
Can you promise
she'll never get caught up in that stuff?

17:30.716 --> 17:33.135
Merry Christmas!

17:33.218 --> 17:35.095
Get your Christmas Cake here!

17:38.766 --> 17:41.518
Shit, it's cold!
It's freaking snowing too!

17:42.478 --> 17:44.897
Hey, Chifuyu. Where the heck's Takemitchy?

17:45.606 --> 17:47.441
He said something came up.

17:47.524 --> 17:48.609
You sure he's okay?

17:48.692 --> 17:50.569
Our plan's supposed to happen tomorrow.

17:51.487 --> 17:52.863
Why don't we get dinner first?

18:04.875 --> 18:05.709
What?

18:09.963 --> 18:12.007
Let's break up, Hina.

18:13.926 --> 18:16.345
I know you're wondering
where this is coming from.

18:17.054 --> 18:19.473
I've kind of been
thinking about it for a while...

18:20.641 --> 18:23.560
I mean, I think I like someone else...

18:24.812 --> 18:27.481
Yeah, that's it. I like someone else.

18:33.487 --> 18:35.322
Hina, I don't...

18:37.741 --> 18:38.951
like you anymore.

18:40.452 --> 18:41.328
So...

18:52.548 --> 18:53.799
Wait! Hina!

18:56.009 --> 18:58.762
I hate you! I hate you! I hate you!

19:06.270 --> 19:07.437
I hate your guts!

19:29.877 --> 19:32.421
Can you promise
she'll never get caught up in that stuff?

19:33.130 --> 19:37.467
<i>There may be some connection
between Kisaki, Hina, and me.</i>

19:38.093 --> 19:39.428
<i>This is for the best.</i>

19:41.972 --> 19:42.931
This is...

19:43.015 --> 19:46.643
It's clear that she really loved you.

19:47.853 --> 19:51.106
You dumped me here... on Christmas Eve.

19:51.690 --> 19:53.400
<i>So, this is what happened.</i>

19:54.484 --> 19:55.485
Tell me why!

19:56.445 --> 19:57.905
<i>This is for the best.</i>

19:58.405 --> 20:00.824
I want to know everything about you.

20:01.408 --> 20:04.369
I'll protect you, Hanagaki!

20:05.454 --> 20:06.496
<i>This is for the best.</i>

20:10.667 --> 20:13.545
There's nobody else as cool as you.

20:18.300 --> 20:20.761
I'm sure you'll succeed, Takemichi.

20:28.018 --> 20:29.228
What'll I do now?

20:31.855 --> 20:33.065
I love her!

20:38.612 --> 20:40.072
Sorry, I'm late.

20:41.198 --> 20:44.243
What's your problem?
Tomorrow's the big day, man!

20:44.326 --> 20:45.452
You're not taking this seriously.

20:46.036 --> 20:47.371
Jeez, Takemitchy,

20:47.454 --> 20:49.248
what's with your face?

20:49.331 --> 20:50.165
What?

20:50.249 --> 20:54.127
Holy shit!
Your ugly mug looks even worse now!

20:58.173 --> 21:02.302
This is going to go down
at Udagawa Christ Church in Shibuya.

21:02.886 --> 21:04.012
<i>Fortunately,</i>

21:04.096 --> 21:06.890
<i>he'll go to worship there
in the dead of night when nobody's around.</i>

21:07.724 --> 21:11.728
<i>Wouldn't a church be full of people
on Christmas night?</i>

21:11.812 --> 21:14.398
<i>That happens tonight, on Christmas Eve.</i>

21:14.481 --> 21:16.358
<i>Around this time tomorrow, it's empty.</i>

21:16.858 --> 21:20.904
If Hakkai's going to attack Taiju,
that has to be when he'll do it.

21:21.405 --> 21:24.449
We'll wait for Taiju
outside the main chapel.

21:24.992 --> 21:27.703
Hakkai should already be inside
waiting for him.

21:27.786 --> 21:29.579
Takemitchy, you have to convince him.

21:30.539 --> 21:31.915
Since you're friends,

21:31.999 --> 21:34.835
you're the best person
to stop Hakkai, right?

21:37.462 --> 21:41.508
And before Hakkai can confront Taiju,
us three outside...

21:42.175 --> 21:43.302
will beat down Taiju.

21:47.723 --> 21:53.020
Well, it looks like our secret operation
against BLACK DRAGON is going to happen.

21:53.103 --> 21:56.565
I don't know what happened to you earlier,
but tomorrow,

21:56.648 --> 21:58.942
you can vent all your anger!

22:03.071 --> 22:03.905
<i>Hina...</i>

22:04.781 --> 22:06.033
<i>This time, for sure,</i>

22:06.116 --> 22:09.202
<i>I'll protect your future.</i>

23:38.375 --> 23:40.377
Translation by Brian Athey
